<title>USA: U.S. Senate Finance bill would raise debt limit.</title>
<headline>U.S. Senate Finance bill would raise debt limit.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Legislation drafted by the Senate Finance Committee chairman on the spending portion of the budget would raise the U.S. debt limit to $5.95 trillion from $5.5 trillion.</p>
<p>Chairman William Roth, a Delaware Republican, has put together legislation to implement spending portions of the balanced budget agreement, including for the Medicare and Medicaid programs.</p>
<p>The committee, citing the Treasury Department, said the proposed increase in the debt limit was expected to last through December 1999.</p>
</text>
